Shares represent interests in the fund, not claims on the sponsor. Sponsor insolvency does not cancel them.\n\n**What can still go wrong:**\n- **Commingling or fraud** can create creditor claims despite the structure.\n- **Affiliated exposures**, such as cash sweeps at sponsor-affiliated banks or securities lending, may be at risk.\n- **Adviser, administrator, or distributor contracts** may terminate, delaying creations and redemptions or forcing board action such as replacement, reorganization, or liquidation.\n- **Index or ticker licenses** may be affected.\n\nOutcomes depend on the facts and documents, so verify against the prospectus, SAI, custody agreement, and sponsor filings. This is general information, not legal advice.","ttft_ms":1479,"type":"result","duration_ms":1497,"uuid":"9b329489-eda2-48de-94da-c34bc33088c7","ttft_stream_ms":391,"time_to_request_ms":51,"first_content_frame_ms":391,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
